  "digest": "# TECHNOLOGY \u2014 sector digest, ISO week 2026-W46\n\n**Coverage changes.** Six technology initiations went live on 12 Nov: GOTO.JK BUY, target Rp53 (+120.8% expected return); BUKA.JK BUY, Rp190 (+84.5%); BELI.JK REDUCE, Rp187.6 (-19.2%); WIFI.JK BUY, Rp5,207; NFCX.JK SELL. All are rated against 5 Nov prices [coverage status]. EMTK.JK's ad hoc BUY, Rp484.9, was parked after failing the QC audit twice and is not published. DCII.JK is unchanged at SELL, Rp87,286 [coverage:DCII.JK]. The desk now has six published names; 51 technology names remain queued and five sit in draft.\n\n**Deck moves.** There is no technology industry deck: all four industries read the macro deck only [operating configuration]. Macro forecasts did not change this week; spot marks were refreshed to 13 Nov with USD/IDR still on the 23-Oct onshore close of Rp18,080 as basis of record, alongside BI rate 5.75% and CPI 3.28% [deck:macro].\n\n**Material news.** MSCI removed EMTK and WIFI from its Global Small Cap index in the November rebalancing, together with AVIA, CTRA, MTEL, JSMR and RAJA [news ce6fdb9748402de8]. MSTI declared an interim dividend of Rp150.69bn and published the schedule [news 49a0aeeca63f509f]. GOTO cancelled its treasury shares after returning to profit, lifting the free-float share of the register [news 339411a9a0d593da]. BUKA was named among names where improving gaming profitability is the catalyst [news d3ee277f9c432845].\n\n**What to watch.** Index-driven flow in EMTK and WIFI after the MSCI deletion; GOTO's liquidity after the treasury cancellation; MSTI's dividend record and payment dates; EMTK's route back through QC and signoff; and the next BI-Rate decision and USD/IDR prints, which set the cost of capital for every name on the desk.\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*",
  "digest_file": "fund record"
